{
  "name": "Section 301 Forced Labor Investigation \u2014 Annex A Product Exemptions (USTR, June 2, 2026)",
  "source": "https://ustr.gov/sites/default/files/files/Press/Releases/2026/FRN%20-%20Section%20301%20Forced%20Labor%20Import%20Ban%20Actionabilty%20and%20Proposed%20Action%206-2-26%20FINAL.pdf",
  "rate": 0.0,
  "notes": [
    "Products listed here are explicitly excluded from the proposed Section 301 action per Annex A of the June 2, 2026 FRN (dockets USTR-2026-0265, USTR-2026-0266).",
    "725 codes covering HTS chapters 02-09 (agricultural/food), 10-22 (processed foods, beverages), 25-27 (minerals, fuels, petroleum products), and 28-29 (inorganic and organic chemicals, pharmaceuticals).",
    "10 codes are 'Ex'-scoped (scope limited to product description, not the full subheading): 0805.90.01, 0811.90.80, 1404.90.90, 1905.90.10, 1905.90.90, 2008.99.21, 2009.31.60, 2009.89.70, 2009.90.40, 2106.90.99. Modeled as fully exempt since trade data contains no description field.",
    "In addition to this list, the following are also excluded from S301 but handled elsewhere in the pipeline: all articles subject to Section 232 tariffs; USMCA-compliant goods; CAFTA-DR duty-free textiles/apparel; informational materials; donations; accompanied baggage."
  ],
